      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSet amidst approximately 5 acres of mature grounds, Ballynagar House, Loughrea, Co. Galway is a magnificent Georgian residence dating from 1807, offering a rare opportunity to restore a truly historic country home to its former splendour. This elegant five-bay, two-storey over basement residence fronts onto an even earlier structure believed to have been constructed in the seventeenth century, providing an extraordinary blend of architectural heritage and character. While the property requires comprehensive renovation, it presents an exceptional canvas for those seeking to create a truly unique family home, seamlessly combining timeless period charm with modern comforts and personal design. Ideally positioned just a short drive from Loughrea Town, the property enjoys the perfect balance of peaceful countryside living and convenient access to a wide range of amenities, including schools, shops, cafés, restaurants and sporting facilities. Excellent transport links via the nearby M6 motorway provide easy access to both Galway City and Dublin, making Ballynagar House an outstanding choice for those seeking a distinguished country residence in a well-connected location.\n\nRich in original features, Ballynagar House retains many of the fine architectural details synonymous with its era, including ornate fireplaces, original skirting boards, architraves, decorative coving, traditional window shutters and numerous other period features that reflect the property's remarkable history. The grounds, extending to approximately 5 acres, have become overgrown and require some restoration, yet offer tremendous potential to create a magnificent estate. Comprising mature woodland, open pasture, a pond and stream, an orchard and traditional stables, the property provides an exceptional opportunity for a discerning purchaser to reinstate the gardens and landscape to their former glory. Whether restored as an elegant private residence, an impressive country retreat or a distinguished family home, Ballynagar House represents a once-in-a-generation opportunity to breathe new life into one of County Galway's finest historic homes.\n\nDesigned by Richard Morrison one of the \npremier early 19th century Irish architects.\n\nThe ground floor boasts a spacious entrance hall, lounge, sitting room, living room, dining room and kitchen. The first-floor features 8 bedrooms and bathroom, the basement features a hallway, kitchen and 3 further rooms.\n\nSERVICES: Well & Septic Tank\nPROPERTY SIZE: 550m\nPROPERTY AGE: 1807\nBUILDING ENERGY RATING: EXEMPT \nNIAH No: 30412515"
      },
